00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:36.910
Far out at sea, a pod of humpback whales was traveling south for the winter.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:42.920
Humpback whales are magnificent creatures that sing to each other underwater.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:49.480
In the whole world, there are very few of them, so each one is quite special.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.700
Every winter, they travel south.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:59.040
Every summer, they head north, and they always know the way.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.260
But even whales can make mistakes.

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:07.700
One day, a whale named Humphrey made a big one.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.750
He turned away from his friends

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:15.480
and wandered under the Golden Gate Bridge into San Francisco Bay.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.560
Everyone was surprised to see Humphrey in the bay.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.940
He was a spectacular sight, as long as a city bus

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:29.650
and as big as seven elephants put together.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:37.700
When he came up to breathe, appearing as if by magic, people would stop whatever they were doing to watch him.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.240
Then, Humphrey did something no whale had ever done.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:51.350
Instead of swimming back out to sea, he went the wrong way, up the Sacramento River.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:58.130
The big river became smaller and smaller as Humphrey traveled upstream.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.210
He was looking for the ocean, but it was clear.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.800
Humphrey was lost.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.360
Hundreds of people came to see Humphrey.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.260
There he is, they shined.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:17.660
He was an amazing sight, but something was wrong.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:21.710
Whales are supposed to live in the salt water of the ocean,

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:24.260
not in the fresh water of rivers.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:29.200
A whale would die if it stayed in fresh water too long.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:32.940
Humphrey was in trouble.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:39.070
The farther Humphrey went, the more worried everyone became.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:45.320
Then one day, Humphrey squeezed under a tiny bridge.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:51.040
It was so small, no one could understand how he had done it.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.310
Now he was really trapped.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:59.290
The river beyond the bridge was very shallow.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.340
Something had to be done to get him out of there.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:06.520
Humphrey looked sick.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:10.650
The scientists knew he would die if he didn't get back to the ocean.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.050
Time was running out.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.320
Scientists, Coast Guard officers, and many others

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:22.220
got together to work out a plan to save Humphrey.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.760
They decided to bang long pipes together underwater

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.540
and scare him back down the river.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:37.910
At the same time, they would play a recording that would broadcast underwater the sounds of whales eating.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:46.130
Maybe Humphrey would be so hungry and lonely, he would swim toward the sound.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:54.050
It worked! Humphrey turned around and started swimming back down the river.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:59.800
Everyone was relieved, but the danger wasn't over yet.

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:08.820
When Humphrey arrived at the little bridge, he stopped, couldn't find a space big enough to go through.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.810
People kept banging the pipes.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.500
Humphrey became angry.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.910
He rolled from side to side and thrashed his great tail.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:25.130
People stopped banging the pipes, but they didn't give up.

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:29.080
They decided to make the space under the bridge bigger.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:37.210
They brought in a huge crane and worked through the night to clear away some of the old pilings.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:41.650
The next day, the people began banging the pipes together again.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.500
The boats moved closer to Humphrey to urge him on toward the bridge.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:53.000
This was his last chance.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.380
Everyone watched nervously.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.860
Humphrey bravely approached the bridge.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:06.310
But as he tried to swim under it, his head became lodged between the pilings.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:12.230
He frantically bobbed his head up and down and thrashed his tail to free himself.

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:20.610
Suddenly, Humphrey lifted one fin way out of the water, almost touching the bridge.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:28.370
As he twisted his body, he broke free from the pilings and swam through to the other side.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:37.180
there was a shout from the riverbank and then another and another until everyone was cheering

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:46.070
hooray for a humphrey they shouted he made it humphrey the lost whale was finally on his way home

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:54.450
a whole flotilla of boats and the clanging of pipes helped humphrey find his way down the river

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.100
Finally, Humphrey arrived at San Francisco Bay.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:04.430
Humphrey spent one whole day happily swimming around the bay.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:08.150
He did tricks for the people gathered along the shore.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:15.730
Humphrey seemed to be saying goodbye and thank you to all his friends who had helped save his life.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:24.960
Finally, in the late afternoon fog, Humphrey swam under the Golden Gate Bridge and back out to sea.

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:28.560
Humphrey the whale had made it.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:44.340
Humphrey's story is about a whale, but it's also about all of the people who cared enough to help him find his way home.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:50.500
The most amazing thing about Humphrey's story is that it really happened.

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:59.160
As Humphrey swam up the Sacramento River, crowds of people came from everywhere to help the experts turn him around.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:06.500
They urged him on as he struggled to swim between the piling under the bridge.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:14.490
There were some tense moments for everyone when it seemed that Humphrey might not make it.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:20.200
And when he finally succeeded, everyone cheered.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:29.980
All the people in the crowd felt they had a small part in Humphrey's success as they watched him...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.460
